# lib/libcss/Makefile -- NetSurf libcss (CSS parser + selector + cascade)
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libcss @ commit 104d87f
# (v0.9.x). Copyright 2007-2021 J-M Bell + Vincent Sanders + others, MIT-
# licensed (see COPYING).
#
# 185 .c files upstream. We exclude TWO from the archive:
#   - src/parse/properties/css_property_parser_gen.c -- it's a build-time
#     code generator with int main(); generates the per-property parser
#     dispatchers that ARE in the archive (committed pre-generated).
#   - src/select/format_list_style.c -- 67 lines of UTF-8 (Georgian /
#     Armenian / Greek alphabet tables for CSS list-style-type counter
#     formatting). bebbo-gcc preprocessor silently corrupts code surrounding
#     multi-byte UTF-8 characters (per known-pitfalls "UTF-8 Characters in
#     Comments Break bebbo-gcc Preprocessor"). NetSurf rendering of MVP
#     HTML+CSS does NOT need exotic counter styles -- it just needs the
#     rest of the cascade. Re-enable later by ASCII-stripping the symbol
#     tables or hex-escaping the codepoints. Tracked in lib/libcss/README.md.
#
# Final OBJS count: 183 .c files / ~30K LOC across:
#   - src/lex/        : CSS tokeniser
#   - src/parse/      : top-level parser
#   - src/parse/properties/ : per-property parser dispatchers (~50 .c files)
#   - src/select/     : selector matcher + cascade + arena
#   - src/select/properties/ : per-property select/cascade dispatchers (~100 .c)
#   - src/charset/    : @charset + BOM detection
#   - src/utils/      : errors, utility helpers
#   - src/stylesheet.c : top-level stylesheet API
#
# Source-analyzer audit verdict: CAVEATS (the format_list_style.c exclusion
# above; everything else CLEAN). No source patches.
#
# CRITICAL design fact: libcss uses 22:10 fixed-point integer math
# (`css_fixed = int32_t` per include/libcss/fpmath.h), NOT floating-point.
# Zero soft-float pulls expected -- verified at Stage 7 perf audit. The
# `FLTTOFIX(0.9)` style macros in property parsers are compile-time
# constants and fold to integers under -O0 (no runtime float ops).
#
# Required by: ports/netsurf (Phase 1 final consumer).
#
# CPU TARGET: -m68040 -m68881 (NetSurf-Vampire dep stack convention; see
# lib/libwapcaplet/Makefile header for rationale).
#
# DEPENDS ON: lib/libwapcaplet, lib/libparserutils (already shipped).
# Link order on consumer side: -lcss -lwapcaplet -lparserutils.

TOOLCHAIN_BIN = ../../toolchain/scripts
CC            = $(TOOLCHAIN_BIN)/m68k-amigaos-gcc
AR            = $(TOOLCHAIN_BIN)/m68k-amigaos-ar
RANLIB        = $(TOOLCHAIN_BIN)/m68k-amigaos-ranlib

# -O1 promoted whole-archive 2026-05-02 after perf-optimizer audit. All
# 302 TUs are -O1-safe per crash-patterns #16:
#   - Zero struct-by-value returns >8 bytes (every libcss API returns
#     by pointer or scalar css_error / css_fixed)
#   - Zero soft-float pulls (verified via m68k-amigaos-nm libcss.a |
#     grep '__\(div\|mul\)\(sf\|df\)3' -- empty -- 22:10 fixed-point
#     integer math throughout)
#   - 5 benign ___divdi3 references for 64-bit integer overflow-prevent
#     in the fixed-point evaluator (NOT crash-risk; libgcc helper)
#   - No large stack arrays; no alignment quirks
# Estimated speedup: 1.3-1.8x render-path cascade, 1.5-2x parse path.
# Same whole-archive pattern as the 4 prior dep stack libs. See
# lib/libcss/PERF-REPORT.md for the full audit.
# -fno-strict-aliasing defensive (prevents aliasing-based misopts on
#   the pointer-heavy property dispatcher tables).
# -m68040 -m68881 matches NetSurf consumer ABI.
# -std=c99 mandatory: source uses bool, uint*_t, designated initialisers.
# -DNDEBUG strips assert() and verbose-debug fprintf paths.
# -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE matches upstream Makefile.
# -I include/ for the public libcss/ headers.
# -I src/ for internal cross-subsystem headers.
# -I lib/libwapcaplet/include for libwapcaplet.h.
# -I lib/libparserutils/include for parserutils types referenced by
#   the lexer + input stream.
CFLAGS  = -O1 -fno-strict-aliasing -noixemul -m68040 -m68881 -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra
CFLAGS += -DNDEBUG -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE
CFLAGS += -Iinclude -Isrc
CFLAGS += -I../../lib/libwapcaplet/include
CFLAGS += -I../../lib/libparserutils/include

TARGET = libcss.a

